course: dictionary
lesson: 2179
title: Names and capital letters
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Cortina is a word with several meanings, and the capital letter is your first clue. A name with a capital letter names one special place, person or thing. This is called a proper noun. «The Winter Olympics in Milan and Cortina, Italy, were in February 2026.» Here Cortina is a town, so the sentence tells you where the Olympics were.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to choose. If the sentence is about a car, a family or an old road trip in Britain, Cortina means the Ford Cortina. If it is about skiing, the Olympics or the mountains of northern Italy, it means the ski town of Cortina d'Ampezzo. Ask yourself: what is the sentence about?
explain: A lowercase cortina is different. In Spanish, «cortina» means a curtain, but that is not an English word in that sense. A rare science meaning, the cobweb-like veil under the cap of some young mushrooms, is seldom used. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
explain: The sentence also gives you clues: «skaters balance using the inner ear, eyes and strong leg and core muscles.» Skaters and the Olympics point to sport, so Cortina here is a place, not a car.
fact: Cortina is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Cortina» can name a car: the Ford Cortina, a very popular family car in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand from 1962 to 1982.
fact: «Cortina d'Ampezzo» is a ski town in the Dolomite mountains of northern Italy.
fact: Cortina d'Ampezzo hosted the Winter Olympics in 1956, and with Milan it hosted them in 2026.
fact: In Spanish, «cortina» means a curtain; it is not an English word in that sense.
exercise: «The Winter Olympics in Milan and Cortina, Italy, were in February 2026.» What is Cortina in this sentence? | A family car | A curtain | *A ski town in Italy
exercise: Ruby's grandad says, «We drove our old Cortina to the seaside.» What is the Cortina? | A ski town in northern Italy | A cobweb-like veil under a mushroom | A curtain in Spanish | *The Ford Cortina car
exercise: Why does the capital letter matter in Cortina? | *It shows it is the name of one special place, car or thing | It shows the word is very old | It shows the word is in Spanish | It shows the word is a question
test: «The skaters trained hard before the Winter Olympics in Cortina.» What does Cortina name here? | A curtain | *A town in Italy | A Ford car | A cobweb
test: In Spanish, «cortina» means what? | A mushroom | A mountain | *A curtain | A car
exam: «The Winter Olympics in Milan and Cortina, Italy, were in February 2026.» Which meaning of Cortina fits best? | A veil under a mushroom cap | *A ski town in the Dolomite mountains | The Ford Cortina car from 1962 | A curtain in a window
